  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "wCDWf7T6NITFAZNGUNHSsMFqG/E=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:22:30.493Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Flowable demo attaches at the two extension points Flowable already exposes to partners: a service task or an event listener, firing at each user-task or case milestone and dispatching a typed operation into Powerhouse. The destructive half is what makes the point \u2014 purge the Flowable instance, then replay the approval chain from Powerhouse. The record of who decided what survives the disappearance of the engine that sequenced it.\n\nThe reuse claim is the reason this note exists separately from the Camunda demo: a Camunda delegate and a Flowable listener are the same integration written twice. The hook name and the SDK differ; the dispatched payload, the typed operation, and the purge-and-replay demonstration do not. Building one and shipping both turns two partner cohorts into one engineering commitment, which changes the economics of addressing either of them individually.\n\nThe cohort is 35 leads, 33 of them mined from the Flowable Partner Finder on 2026-08-18, concentrated in Switzerland and Germany with a long US tail and single entries in FI, EE, IE, TR, IL, IN and CN. The priority distribution is late: 16 at \"3 \u00b7 later\", 13 at \"9 \u00b7 do not pitch\", three at \"2 \u00b7 next\" and three unprioritised. That skew is what makes shared engineering the operative argument \u2014 the cohort is worth serving cheaply rather than worth chasing hard.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (35)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- Creetion (NL Breda) \u2014 creetion.com\n- Masoona Consulting GmbH (DE Nuremberg) \u2014 masoona.de\n- XTi NV (BE Kontich/Hasselt/Merelbeke) \u2014 xt-i.com\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Counterpoint Consulting (US Reston VA) \u2014 counterpointconsulting.com\n- Digital Workforce (FI Helsinki) \u2014 digitalworkforce.com\n- ELCA Group (CH Pully/Lausanne + 4 cities) \u2014 elca.ch\n- Eraneos (CH Zurich) \u2014 eraneos.com\n- Fincons Group (IT Milan + CH/DE/FR/UK/US) \u2014 finconsgroup.com\n- Forty2 AG (CH Cham/Zug + DE/LU/PT/ES) \u2014 forty2.ch\n- GFT Technologies SE (DE Stuttgart + IT/PL delivery) \u2014 gft.com\n- Groupe Onepoint (FR Paris + 7 cities) \u2014 groupeonepoint.com\n- LionGate AG (DE Munich) \u2014 liongate.de\n- Mesoneer AG (CH Zurich) \u2014 mesoneer.io\n- Nortal (EE Tallinn) \u2014 nortal.com\n- Pragmatica AG (CH + EU/SG/HK) \u2014 pragmatica.ch\n- Synpulse (CH Zurich) \u2014 synpulse.com\n- adesso Group (CH Zurich + DE + AT) \u2014 adesso.ch\n- it-novum GmbH (DE Fulda) \u2014 eim.it-novum.com\n- ti&m AG (CH Zurich + Bern/Basel/Frankfurt/Duesseldorf) \u2014 ti8m.com\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Accenture (IE Dublin / global) \u2014 accenture.com\n- BehaimITS (US Chicago IL) \u2014 behaimits.com\n- Clarium (US Miami FL) \u2014 clarium.tech\n- EPAM Systems (US Newtown PA / global) \u2014 epam.com\n- ERRY (CN Shanghai) \u2014 erry.com\n- Fulcrum Digital (US Jersey City NJ) \u2014 fulcrumdigital.com\n- Kurulum (TR Istanbul) \u2014 kurul.com.tr\n- Merkle (dentsu) (US Columbia MD) \u2014 merkle.com\n- Myridius (US Princeton NJ) \u2014 myridius.com\n- Perficient (US St. Louis MO) \u2014 perficient.com\n- STP house (IL Netanya) \u2014 stphouse.com\n- Tata Consultancy Services (IN Mumbai / global) \u2014 tcs.com\n- dxdy (US + LK/SG) \u2014 dxdydigital.com\n\n**unprioritised**\n- Avaloq (CH Zurich) \u2014 avaloq.com\n- Exentra GmbH (DE) \u2014 exentra.de\n- eligamo AG (CH) \u2014 eligamo.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Flowable service task / event listener dispatching a typed operation at each user-task or case milestone. Then purge the Flowable instance and replay the approval chain from Powerhouse. A Camunda delegate and a Flowable listener are the same integration twice \u2014 build one, ship both.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:22:30.493673Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:22:30.493676Z"
    }
  },
